  "python_conversion_notes": "Two custom indicators (emaangle, Laguerre_RSI_with_Laguerre_filter) must be reimplemented in Python since iCustom calls require MT5 terminal. The EMAAngle indicator reads buffer 0 at shift 1 (previous bar). The Laguerre RSI indicator reads buffer 2 at shift 0 (current bar). CMoneyFixedMargin logic needs replication - it calculates lot size based on fixed margin risk percentage. The grid step logic (ExtStepGrid) checks distance from lowest BUY / highest SELL before allowing new entries. The daily loss counter scans deal history which requires trade history access in Python. Filling type auto-detection (FOK/IOC/RETURN) needs broker-specific handling. Trailing stop is implemented inline in CheckOpenPositions (active) but also as unused standalone Trailing() function. The position_gate logic is nuanced: EMAAngle direction determines which side can trade, but only if opposite side has zero positions.",
